all, additional filtering methods give users more options and choice. Perhaps someone needs to use stretched textures viewed from a distance. In that case, anisotropic filtering will provide better quality. The documentation should specify that anisotropic filtering is suitable for stretched textures. Otherwise, anisotropic filtering is pointless, as it doesn't improve quality and slightly degrades performance.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451820365/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451831103","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112051#issuecomment-3451831103","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112051","id":3451831103,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NvsM_","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T15:17:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T15:17:49Z","body":"What are the use case where 2D textures are stretched like this? This isn't about 3D rendering where this is relevant, but for 2D, in what situation would the engine render 2D textures in a stretched way?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451831103/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451872217","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112051#issuecomment-3451872217","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112051","id":3451872217,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nv2PZ","user":{"login":"PavielKraskouski","id":9061796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjE3OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9061796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski","html_url":"https://github.com/PavielKraskouski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T15:24:35Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T15:24:35Z","body":"What I'm referring to is when 2D textures are scaled unevenly along two axes, meaning the texture is stretched. I might be wrong, but in this case, screen pixels will be projected onto texture texels as a rectangular area. To make the texture appear sharper, you need to use multiple samples along the long side of the rectangular projection. This is what anisotropic filtering does.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451872217/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451882972","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112051#issuecomment-3451882972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112051","id":3451882972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nv43c","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T15:26:26Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T15:26:26Z","body":"Yes I know, I'm asking *where* that would happen, what situation would there be where *all* 2D textures in a scene would need this, rather than specific cases, or when would it be needed to do this as a project wide setting?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451882972/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451949402","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112051#issuecomment-3451949402","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112051","id":3451949402,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NwJFa","user":{"login":"PavielKraskouski","id":9061796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjE3OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9061796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski","html_url":"https://github.com/PavielKraskouski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PavielKraskouski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T15:36:43Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T15:36:43Z","body":"Unfortunately, we can't know in advance which game or program will need this. If I understand correctly, it's still possible to enable anisotropic filtering for the entire project via code. This PR doesn't add anything new. It simply makes it easier to enable anisotropic filtering for the entire project using the GUI. In any case, anisotropic filtering shouldn't be enabled by default. I think most users won't change the default filtering settings at all. But this will allow other users with specific projects to enable anisotropic filtering.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3451949402/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3452835637","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112051#issuecomment-3452835637","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112051","id":3452835637,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nzhc1","user":{"login":"RebelliousX","id":1888186,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4ODgxODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1888186?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX","html_url":"https://github.com/RebelliousX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T18:55:05Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T18:55:05Z","body":"Can someone explain why we have this option if Anisotropic filtering is not allowed in Texture Filterin?\r\n<img width=\"985\" height=\"167\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3268710c-57ba-45ff-9f6d-b70b62e71ba9\" />\r\n\r\nFor months I thought I had Anisotropic filtering enabled by choosing 16x. Apparently not. \r\n\r\nI would argue if this PR does not get merged then this option needs to be removed since it is misleading and will let users think they enabled Anisotropic filtering when in fact, it doesn't do anything by itself.\r\n\r\nAgain, for anyone who says Anisotropic filtering is not needed, here is the comparison (uploaded them again 😄) Click on them to expand them and see the difference. It is a 2D project.\r\n<img width=\"1627\" height=\"743\" alt=\"Windowed 720p\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d44d0598-de90-4204-8d32-ba3aa66e517b\" />\r\n<img width=\"2303\" height=\"1078\" alt=\"Fullscreen 1080p\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ff9d87f-3ecb-41ed-a3bf-c7fc40d4290c\" />\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3452835637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3452850830","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112051#issuecomment-3452850830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112051","id":3452850830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NzlKO","user":{"login":"RebelliousX","id":1888186,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4ODgxODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1888186?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RebelliousX","html_url":"https://github.com/RebelliousX"